//
// Description : PROTOTYPE of a library host class: a cFTLocalWebControlHost laid out on a grid the way
//               a Windows dialog is - controls at their natural size, the extra space where it stretches.
//
// This code is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY;
// without even the implied warranty of MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.
//****************************************************************************
Use cFTLocalWebControlHost.pkg

/* THE GRID HOST - a prototype, to move into the library once it holds up.

   Laid out the way a Windows dialog is (Nils 2026-09-27: "we are really building a Windows
   application"): every control keeps its natural size, and the extra space goes where the window
   should stretch - not the framework's resize-for-every-device model, where a width is a share of
   the window.

   - peLayoutType ltGrid: a control sits in a column AND a row - piColumnIndex and piRowIndex (both
     count from 0), piColumnSpan and piRowSpan.
   - psDefaultColumnWidth "max-content": a column is as wide as its widest control. piColumnCount is
     the number of columns the layout uses, in order.
   - psDefaultRowHeight: a row is as tall as its tallest control, and never less than one FT row
     (--ft-row), so an empty row keeps the height of a row of buttons.

   The object says where the window stretches: psColumnWidths "4/1fr" gives column 4 the extra width
   (an empty column before right-hand buttons, or a field that grows); psRowHeights "1/1fr" gives row 1
   the extra height (a page or a list, with pbFillHeight). Pixels ("3/16") only for a deliberate gap.
   Never percentages: they are a share of the WHOLE height and ignore the other rows. A width entry
   past piColumnCount is ignored.

   Anchors, translated:
     a button that keeps its size        its own max-content column
     buttons anchored bottom-right       a 1fr column before them, in a row below the 1fr row
     a field anchored left and right     its column is 1fr
     a page anchored on all sides        in the 1fr column and the 1fr row, with pbFillHeight

   The grid trap: piColumnSpan 0 means ONE column here, not "the rest of the row" as in the flow
   layout - a control that spans the width says how many columns.

   The OverrideProperty tags tell the Studio these are the class's own defaults, so its Designer and
   property panel show them; the Sets make them so at run time. */
{ OverrideProperty=peLayoutType InitialValue=ltGrid }
{ OverrideProperty=psDefaultColumnWidth InitialValue="max-content" }
Class cDemoGridHost is a cFTLocalWebControlHost
    Procedure Construct_Object
        Forward Send Construct_Object

        Set peLayoutType to ltGrid
        Set psDefaultColumnWidth to "max-content"
        Set psDefaultRowHeight to "minmax(var(--ft-row, 33px), max-content)"
    End_Procedure
End_Class
